From: Mirko Vogt <foss@mirko.in>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 02:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2-request: define sunxi AFBC pixelformats when the headers lack them

The cedrus 8-bit/10-bit AFBC capture formats
(V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_{8,10}_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT) are downstream additions, not
in mainline videodev2.h. OpenWrt packages build against the sanitized
toolchain kernel-headers, which therefore lack these fourccs, so the table
entries guarded by "#if defined(...)" are compiled out and 10-bit HEVC never
gets a DRM_PRIME capture format (hwaccel init fails, ffmpeg silently falls
back to software decoding).

Define the fourccs in this translation unit when the headers do not; the
values match the kernel UAPI (drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus).

Signed-off-by: Mirko Vogt <foss@mirko.in>
---
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -34,6 +34,18 @@
 #include "hwcontext_v4l2request_internal.h"
 #include "mem.h"
 
+/* The sunxi/cedrus AFBC pixelformats are downstream additions (not in
+ * mainline videodev2.h), so sanitized toolchain kernel-headers lack them and
+ * the capture format table below would be compiled without them. Define them
+ * when absent; the values must match the kernel UAPI. */
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_8_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_8_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT  v4l2_fourcc('A', 'S', '1', '2')
+#endif
+
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT v4l2_fourcc('A', 'S', '0', '1')
+#endif
+
 typedef struct V4L2RequestVideoDecoder {
     dev_t media_dev;
     dev_t video_dev;
